IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://houstonarboretum.o
 rg/wp-content/uploads/2023/05/Grazing-Goats-Anthony-Rathbun-1280-x-720.jpg
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://houstonarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2
 023/05/Grazing-Goats-Anthony-Rathbun-1280-x-720.jpg
UID:IjAftWfxtsuBCNziuPIEf
SUMMARY:Goats at the Arboretum
DTSTAMP:20260717T141414Z
DTSTART:20260803T070000Z
DESCRIPTION:August 3-10\, 2026 – Dates are subject to change. Please check 
	back for updates.7:00 am – 7:30 pm \n\n\n\nGoats from GoatScaping LLC will
	 be at the Arboretum this August clearing out invasive and aggressive nati
	ve understory brush and vegetation to allow for increased biodiversity! Th
	is year\, the goats will be working on a 7 acre area in the northwest corn
	er of the Arboretum between the 610 Parking Loop\, the Ravine Trail\, and 
	the Event Lawn. Read below for some helpful tips for viewing the goats at 
	work! \n\n\n\nAre you an Arboretum Member? If so\, join us on Friday\, Aug
	ust 7 from 10:00 am – 12:00 pm for a fun\, free Members-only Meet the Mowe
	rs event! \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n2026 Goat visit map\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nGoat View
	ing Tips\n\n\n\n\nPark at either entrance and follow the yellow arrows alo
	ng the trails directing you from the Nature Center to the goats’ current l
	ocation. You can also look at the Goat Visit Map to plan your walk.\n\n\n\
	nStay on sidewalks and trails.\n\n\n\nKeep children and dogs away from the
	 fence – it is electrified to keep predators like coyotes out of the area.
	\n\n\n\nDo not try to feed or pet the goats. They are helping us clear spe
	cies like poison ivy\, and the oils can get on your skin.\n\n\n\nTake lots
	 of photos – if you post them on social media\, tag @houstonarboretum so w
	e can see them!\n\nhttps://houstonarboretum.org/event/goats-at-the-arboret
	um/\n\nFrom Houston Arboretum & Nature Center
URL:https://houstonarboretum.org/event/goats-at-the-arboretum/
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:houston-arboretum
CATEGORIES:Houston Arboretum & Nature Center
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT181H
END:VEVENT
